 "system": {
  "description": {
   "value": "<p><em>Rot — Innate Technique (11th level)</em></p><p>At 11th level, you learn to condense your blood into wings resembling veins as a bonus action for 8 CE, gaining the following benefits for 1 minute:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>\n<p>Your movement  is quadrupled  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You gain a flying speed equal to half your movement  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You gain advantage on Dexterity saving throws  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>You can replace an attack on your turn with a Rot Technique or one line of blood attack.  </p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p>As a free action on your turn, you can unleash lines of blood.</p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<p>These lines of blood take the shape of three ranged Cursed Energy attacks against a target within 60 feet. Each attack deals 4d10 + your CE modifier acid or necrotic damage. You can also replace an attack on your turn with a line of blood attack. While using Wing King, you cannot use Decay.</p>",
